# Intent: A separate image kind, cloudtest, for trying the vendor's hosted brain with the owner's own account (never the default, never in a release image). With MAIPAI_CLOUDTEST the unit runs the vendor activation check against the upstream address of the pinned xiaozhi-esp32 tree (set only by sdkconfig.cloudtest.defaults), shows the activation code on screen silently (the normal build reboots into the phone-app setup instead), keeps the vendor link's address and token in their own namespaces (cl_websocket, cl_mqtt) so the paired host's pairing is never overwritten, never installs firmware from the vendor service, speaks websocket only, lets the vendor service call only four generic tools (device status, volume, brightness, theme: the privacy, lock, update, asset, game and pantry tools stay out of its reach), and keeps an amber strip "Cloud brain test" on screen. The unit's own mute, full quiet and vision-off bits still decide what the microphone and camera can do. Voice leaves the home while it is connected.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: main/ota.cc, ota.h, application.cc, mcp_server.cc and protocols/websocket_protocol.cc of the xiaozhi-esp32 tree (MIT); firmware/main/hal/maipai_cloudtest.cc and .h (ours)
# Check after a flash: only after the owner has said yes to contacting the vendor service (docs/plan/cloud-brain-firmware-test.md): the strip shows, the log shows the OTA check, an activation code shows on the screen with no sound, entering it in the owner's own console connects the unit, mute and full quiet still stop the microphone, and a flash of the plain image brings the host link back with the old pairing.
# Kconfig: MAIPAI_CLOUDTEST (default n); the kind sets STACKCHAN_OTA_CHECK and OTA_URL
# Memory cost: none in any other kind (everything is behind MAIPAI_CLOUDTEST). In the cloudtest kind: one esp_timer and a 16 px strip on the system layer, about 1 KB internal RAM, and the vendor check task with its 8 KB stack at start-up (stock behavior).

